t\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" fall asleep\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" break up\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" end a relationship\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "You <span class=\"strong\">passed out </span>before the couple decided to break up.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I was <span class=\"strong\">taken aback</span> by how shallow the characters were.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I didn't <span class=\"strong\">nod off</span> did I?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Actually, I was <span class=\"strong\">taken aback</span> by how shallow the characters were.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The things they <span class=\"strong\">came out with</span>!", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Negative Questions to Encourage Agreement", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use negative questions to confirm information you already know.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">Wasn't it romantic?</span> <br /> You think it was romantic and you expect the answer to be 'yes'. You expect the person you are talking to will share your opinion. <br /><br /> <span class=\"italic\">Aren't we going out to eat now?</span> <br /> You expect to eat now and you expect that the other person will agree with you.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Wasn't it romantic?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Aren't we going out to eat now?", "type": "example"}, {"content": " Isn't it a beautiful evening?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Don't you think the skyline is very romantic?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Didn't you say it was just around the corner?", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to snore", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to breathe loudly while sleeping", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content":